.TH LIBRDP-VIEWER 1 "2026-07-19" "librdp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
librdp-viewer \- native RDP client viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B librdp-viewer
.B --target
.I host
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B librdp-viewer
connects to an RDP target, presents framebuffer updates, forwards keyboard and
pointer input, and exposes optional device and media feature paths through the
public librdp client API. CMake builds the Cocoa frontend on macOS and the X11
frontend on the supported non-Apple systems.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --target " host"
Remote host name or address.
.TP
.BI --port " port"
Remote TCP port. The default is 3389.
.TP
.BI --user " name"
User name for authentication.
.TP
.BI --password " value"
Password for authentication. Avoid placing credentials in shell history on shared systems.
.TP
.BI --domain " name"
Authentication domain.
.TP
.BI --width " px"
Initial desktop width.
.TP
.BI --height " px"
Initial desktop height.
.TP
.BI --security " auto|rdp|tls|nla"
Security negotiation mode.
.TP
.B --tls-prompt-cert
Show the presented TLS leaf certificate and ask whether to accept it for the current connection.
.TP
.B --tls-accept-any-cert
Accept the presented TLS leaf certificate for the current connection without prompting. This is an explicit trust-policy override for controlled environments.
.TP
.BI --gateway " url"
Tunnel the target TCP connection through an HTTP CONNECT gateway. The URL may use
.B http
or
.B https .
.TP
.BI --gateway-mode " http-connect|rdg-http"
Select the gateway transport. The default is
.BR http-connect .
.B rdg-http
selects Microsoft RD Gateway HTTP transport, creates the RDG OUT/IN streams, and carries the target RDP connection through the negotiated RDG channel.
.TP
.BI --gateway-user " name"
Gateway authentication user name. If omitted, the viewer reuses the session user name when gateway credential reuse is enabled.
.TP
.BI --gateway-password " value"
Gateway authentication password. Avoid placing credentials in shell history on shared systems.
.TP
.BI --gateway-domain " name"
Gateway authentication domain.
.TP
.BI --gateway-timeout " ms"
Gateway connection timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
.B --gateway-no-session-credentials
Do not reuse the session credentials for gateway authentication when dedicated gateway credentials are not provided.
.TP
.BI --drive " name=path"
Redirect a local directory as a remote drive.
.TP
.BI --serial " name=path"
Redirect a local serial endpoint.
.TP
.BI --parallel " name=path"
Redirect a local parallel endpoint.
.TP
.BI --printer " name=driver=path"
Configure printer redirection with output path.
.TP
.BI --clipboard-file " path"
Expose a local file through clipboard file-transfer behavior. This option is
available in the X11 frontend.
.TP
.BI --audio-output " [device=name]"
Enable audio output. The X11 frontend uses PipeWire when available; the macOS
frontend uses Core Audio.
.TP
.BI --audio-input " [device=name]"
Enable audio input. The X11 frontend uses PipeWire when available; the macOS
frontend uses Core Audio.
.TP
.BI --video " file=path"
Enable video output handling and write payloads to a file sink.
.TP
.BI --camera " source"
Enable camera capture. X11 accepts
.BR device=/dev/videoN .
macOS accepts
.BR device=default ,
.B device=id
or
.BR file=path .
.TP
.BI --smartcard " selector"
Enable smartcard redirection through PC/SC or a controlled source supported by
the selected native frontend.
.TP
.BI --usb " vid:pid|bus:dev"
Enable USB redirection for the selected local device.
.TP
.B --pnp
Enable plug-and-play device redirection behavior without auto-announcing local
host devices.
.TP
.BI --webauthn " selector"
Enable WebAuthn redirection through libfido2 or a controlled provider supported
by the selected native frontend.
.TP
.BI --webauthn-rp-id " id"
Add a WebAuthn relying-party identifier allowlist entry. At least one RP ID is required when WebAuthn is enabled.
.TP
.BI --rail " app=path"
Configure a remote application request.
.TP
.B --cr2
Enable composited remoting behavior.
.TP
.B --echo
Enable the echo diagnostics channel.
.TP
.B --telemetry
Enable telemetry channel probing when a privacy-safe runtime path is available.
.TP
.B --multitransport
Enable multitransport probing when a runtime transport provider is available.
.SH NATIVE FRONTENDS
On X11, keyboard translation uses XKB, framebuffer presentation uses XImage or
MIT-SHM, monitor layout uses XRandR when available, and optional local media
uses PipeWire and V4L2. The viewer supports Xwayland keyboard-grab policy.
.PP
On macOS, AppKit and CoreGraphics provide windowing, input, cursor,
framebuffer, and pasteboard integration. Core Audio provides media streams and
AVFoundation provides live camera capture. Native permission prompts are shown
only for operations that require them.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_CLIENT
Enable client, viewer, surface, input, channel, audio, video, and backend trace events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_TRANSPORT
Enable TCP, TLS, UDP, read, write, wait, timeout, and close trace events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_PROTOCOL
Enable handshake, parser, PDU, capability, slow-path, fast-path, channel, and codec trace events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_LEVEL
Set trace verbosity: error, warn, info, debug, trace, or the numeric values 0 through 4.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_HEX_BYTES
Set the maximum number of bytes emitted by bounded protocol hexdumps.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
librdp-viewer --target host --user user --password password --security nla --width 1024 --height 768

librdp-viewer --target host --security nla --gateway https://gateway.example.com/

LIBRDP_TRACE_CLIENT=1 LIBRDP_TRACE_PROTOCOL=1 librdp-viewer --target host --security nla
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp (7),
.BR librdp-api (7),
.BR librdp-tracing (7)
